{"name":"Herald of Spring","hex":"#a46366","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"herald","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A messenger, especially one bringing important news.","A harbinger, giving signs of things to come."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To proclaim or announce an event.","To greet something with excitement; to hail."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herald"},{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Herald","blocks":[{"text":"A herald, or a herald of arms, is an officer of arms, ranking between pursuivant and king of arms. The title is commonly applied more broadly to all officers of arms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Str%C3%B6hl_Heraldischer_Atlas_t01_3.jpg/330px-Str%C3%B6hl_Heraldischer_Atlas_t01_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herald","wikidata":"Q696819"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_King%27s_Coronation_%2852874898271%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_King%27s_Coronation_%2852874898271%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_King%27s_Coronation_%2852874898271%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-The_King%27s_Coronation_%2852874898271%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_King%27s_Coronation_%2852874898271%29_%28cropped